    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d801-a1">

                <pb facs="0760" n="644" xml:id="pg644"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Seoul to the American
                        Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3582 E.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate General</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 7, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my letter of December 9,
                    1910, (No. 1754), addressed to Mr. Schuyler,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d801-f1"/> and
                    to Mr. O’Brien’s reply thereto, of February 7, 1911, (C. No. 1514),<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d801-f2"/> relating to the investigation of lands by the Government
                    of Chosen, I have the honor to enclose herewith circulars, which have been this
                    day issued to foreign owners of land and their agents by the Land Investigation
                    Committee at Seoul, containing instructions to aid in said investigation.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. H. Scidmore.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
